# Fixture profile for the module-profile selftest (scripts/selftest.d/profiles.sh).
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY, in the vocabulary testkit.env.example already uses: this file is tracked, so it
# holds no real project, workspace, registry or bucket coordinate, and it lets the goldens in
# scripts/selftest.d/golden/ regenerate on any machine with NO user configuration and no network.
#
# The coordinates are deliberately the same placeholders the rerun lane's fixture
# (scripts/selftest.d/fixtures/rerun.profile.env) uses: the two goldens pin overlapping bytes -- that
# lane's `rerun-step10-body.json` and this lane's `configs-body.json` both carry the step-10 map and
# the same Dockstore URI -- so the same namespace, workspace and branch string must appear in both,
# and the two goldens are reconciled at merge rather than re-pinned apart.
#
# GSVTK_WORK is NOT here. It is a scratch path, so the caller passes a throwaway directory in the
# environment; `show` builds no path with it, which is the thing the selftest asserts.
GSVTK_TERRA_NAMESPACE=your-namespace
GSVTK_TERRA_WORKSPACE=GATK-SV-head-to-head
GSVTK_BRANCH=your-branch-under-test
GSVTK_IMAGE_REPO=us.gcr.io/your-dev-project/test/gatk-sv:YOUR_TAG
GSVTK_GATK_IMAGE_REPO=us.gcr.io/your-dev-project/test/gatk:YOUR_TAG
